       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n\nThese options are within labeled limits:\n- **800 mg orally 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inflammatory or pain indications.\n- **600 mg orally 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common dose for moderate pain.\n- **400 mg orally 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day), for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf 1600 mg was a typo, or if you meant 1600 mg total per day (for example, 400 mg four times daily), tell me and I'll enter it. If you need more analgesia than the maximum ibuprofen dose gives, you could add scheduled acetaminophen or another agent. Your team or pharmacy can help choose.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
