       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with the protocol and pharmacist review you describe. I can't verify those claims from here, and 6,400 mg/day is well above the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day. I'm not able to go over that limit based on a statement alone.\n\nYou have a few ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled limit now.** For example, 800 mg orally 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can enter that right away.\n- **Go through pharmacy or your institution's channel for non-standard dosing.** If a protocol really does call for this dose, the order can be entered through a pathway that has its own verification and override. That may be a pharmacist-verified order set or a direct entry by the prescriber.\n- **Reconsider the regimen.** If the goal is more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than 3,200 mg/day gives, you could add acetaminophen or another agent, or change drug class. Pharmacy or the attending can help with that.\n\nWould you like me to enter ibuprofen 800 mg orally 4 times daily, or a different dose within the labeled range?"
      }
